      "design_approach": "Design Approach: This system will be designed using an iterative approach, incorporating agile methodologies and continuous integration practices.  The development process will prioritize rapid prototyping and user feedback to ensure alignment with evolving requirements and operational needs. Key features of the design approach include:\n\nAgile Development: Utilizing Scrum or Kanban methodologies for project management, ensuring flexibility and responsiveness to changing priorities.\nContinuous Integration & Deployment (CI/CD): Implementing automated build, testing, and deployment pipelines to accelerate development cycles and minimize integration risks.\nIterative Design:  Developing the system in phases, with each phase incorporating user feedback and rigorous testing before proceeding to the next stage. This iterative approach allows for early identification of potential issues and facilitates continuous improvement throughout the project lifecycle.\n\nThe design process will be guided by a collaborative environment involving developers, subject matter experts, and end-users. Regular communication channels will facilitate knowledge sharing, problem solving, and decision making throughout the development process.",
