      "architectural_decisions": "Key Architectural Decisions\n\nThis section outlines the key architectural decisions made for the R&D software project, which will be crucial to achieving its objectives and meeting user needs. These decisions are based on a thorough analysis of the project's requirements and constraints, as well as an understanding of existing technologies and best practices in defence R&D software development.\n\nModular Architecture: The system is designed using a modular architecture to facilitate independent development, testing, and deployment of individual components. This approach allows for greater flexibility and scalability, enabling the project team to adapt to changing requirements and prioritize specific functionalities.\n\nCloud-Based Infrastructure:  The R&D software will leverage cloud-based infrastructure for its core functionality. This decision was made due to the advantages it offers in terms of scalability, cost efficiency, and access to advanced computing resources. The chosen cloud provider will be selected based on factors such as security, reliability, and compliance with relevant regulations.\n\nSecure Data Handling:  The system prioritizes data security throughout its lifecycle. This includes implementing robust encryption protocols for all sensitive information, adhering to strict data governance policies, and employing multi-factor authentication for user access control. The chosen security measures will be regularly reviewed and updated to ensure compliance with evolving threats and regulations.\n\nOpen Source Integration:  The system will integrate with open source tools and libraries where appropriate to leverage existing functionalities and reduce development time. This approach allows for greater flexibility, faster innovation, and reduced costs while maintaining a high level of security and reliability.\n\nThese key architectural decisions are essential for achieving the project's goals and ensuring its long-term success. The SDD will further detail each decision with specific implementation plans and considerations."
    },
