      "data_structures": "Interface Design - Shared Data Structures\n\n4.1 Overview\n\nThis section details the shared data structures that will be utilized by various components of the R&D software project. These structures are designed to facilitate efficient communication and data exchange between different modules, ensuring interoperability and seamless integration.\n\n4.2 Data Structure Definitions\n\nTelemetry Sample Envelopes:  The ground segment interface transmits telemetry sample envelopes as defined in api.proto (message TelemetrySample). This message format will be used to represent sensor readings for transmission to the ground segment.\n    * REQ-0101: The ground segment interface shall transmit telemetry sample envelopes as defined in api.proto (message TelemetrySample).\n\nAcquisition Command:  The acquisition command interface accepts a StartCommand message to initiate the acquisition process. This message contains information about the number of channels and the desired sample rate.\n    * REQ-0102: The acquisition command interface shall accept a StartCommand message to begin acquisition.\n\nHealth Report:  The health reporting interface exposes an MTBF estimate as defined in api.proto (message HealthReport). This report provides information about the sensor's operational status and estimated Mean Time Between Failures.\n    * REQ-0103: The health reporting interface shall expose an MTBF estimate as defined in api.proto (message HealthReport).\n\n4.3 Data Structure Implementation\n\nThe implementation of these data structures will be based on the following principles:\n\nModularity:  Data structures should be designed to be modular and reusable across different components of the software project.\nEfficiency:  Structures should be optimized for efficient storage and retrieval of data, minimizing memory footprint and processing overhead.\nInteroperability:  Data structures should adhere to established protocols and standards to ensure seamless communication between different modules.\n\n4.4 Data Structure Usage\n\nThe shared data structures will be utilized by various components of the R&D software project, including:\n\nGround Segment Interface:  Transmits telemetry sample envelopes to the ground segment.\nAcquisition Command Interface:  Receives and processes acquisition command messages.\nHealth Reporting Interface:  Exposes MTBF estimates for sensor health reporting.\nSensor Interface:  Provides raw sample streams at the configured sample rate.\n\n4.5 Future Considerations\n\nFuture development of the R&D software project may require additional data structures to support new functionalities and features. These future considerations will be addressed in subsequent iterations of the SDD."
    },
